     SPDX-License-Identifier: Apache-2.0

     Declares the ColorOS/OxygenOS vendor permissions that stock ships inside
     system_ext/framework/oplus-framework-res.apk (package "oplus"), which is
     not present on AOSP-based builds.

     Ported oplus apps (Gallery, AIUnit, Camera, ...) both request these and
     protect their own exported components with them. Without a declaring
     package the permissions do not exist, so every request silently resolves
     to "not granted" and every guarded component rejects all callers: e.g.
     Gallery binding AIUnitDownloadService fails with a Permission Denial.

     Protection levels are copied verbatim from stock. The signature-level
     permissions are granted to the ported apps because this package and they
     are all signed with the platform certificate.

     android.permission.* entries that stock also redeclares here are
     deliberately omitted: AOSP already owns them.
-->
